            <div class="faq">
                <h2>FAQ</h2>
                <h3>Q1.What is the difference between stocks and cryptocurrencies?</h3>
                <p>Stocks represent shares of ownership in a company. 
                    When you buy stock, you are purchasing a piece of that company 
                    and can benefit from dividends and potential growth.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Cryptocurrencies are digital or virtual currencies that use 
                    cryptography for security. They are decentralized and operate on 
                    blockchain technology, which makes them different from traditional 
                    currencies or stocks.
                </p>
                <h3>Q2. How do I start trading stocks and crypto on this platform?</h3>
                <p>
                    To start trading on our platform simply go into the investment page
                    you wish to use (i.e. Stock Invest or Crypto Invest). Once you are 
                    are in the page scroll though our range of investment options or search
                    for your desired one. When you find one you like click into it for further 
                    information and then click invest. Then all thats left to do is select your
                    investment amount and click "Buy". All of your investments will be displayed
                    on the "My Investments" page.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
